<str>
<>

.. Command flags
-silent
-debug ..gives debug recources such as compile speed and runtimes used etc etc, not good inside ides or debuggers/other compilers than usc
-force ..forces the main function to immediately kill the program (unsafe)
-bypass ..allows other functions to end the program when wanted

.. Combined example
void func process(params) <int> {
    if params == true {
        std.out("Processing...")
        retreat
    } else {
        kill -silent -bypass ..bypass allows kill to be forced through something other than the main function
    }
}